<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all font-family="'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" />
      <mj-text font-size="16px" color="#333333" line-height="24px" />
      <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="20px" />
      <mj-button
        background-color="#7E317B"
        color="#ffffff"
        font-weight="bold"
        border-radius="4px"
      />
    </mj-attributes>
    <mj-style>
      .header-text {
        letter-spacing: 2px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }
      li {
        margin-bottom: 8px;
      }
      .exec-table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin-top: 10px;
      }
      .exec-table td {
        padding: 8px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
        font-size: 14px;
      }
      .role-name {
        font-weight: bold;
        color: #7e317b;
        width: 40%;
      }
    </mj-style>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body background-color="#f4f4f4">
    <mj-section background-color="#7E317B" padding="40px 20px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image
          width="300px"
          src="https://harryrich02.github.io/DUMC/img/dumcCrest.png"
          alt="DUMC Crest"
        />
        <mj-text
          align="center"
          color="#ffffff"
          font-size="28px"
          font-weight="900"
          css-class="header-text"
        >
          WAD WEEKLY
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding-top="30px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text>
          Hello and welcome to the first WAD Weekly of the year! To those new here: this is our weekly newsletter and roundup of the club. I'd like to say it's always a good read, but I can't promise anything. To those returning: welcome back unc. And to those who have no idea why they're still on this list: you'll never leave mwahahah.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding-bottom="0px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="22px" font-weight="bold" color="#7E317B"
          >📅 COMING UP</mj-text
        >
        <mj-divider border-width="2px" border-color="#7E317B" />
        <mj-text>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Wed 8:00pm:</strong> Roped-up Social (Jobo)</li>
            <li><strong>Thu 8:00pm:</strong> Team Training (DCC)</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Mon 7:30pm:</strong> Beer & Boulder (DCC + The Water
              House)
            </li>
          </ul>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section background-color="#fafafa">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="22px" font-weight="bold" color="#7E317B"
          >🧗 SUMMER IN THE DUMC</mj-text
        >
        <mj-divider border-width="2px" border-color="#7E317B" />

        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold"
          >Exec Adventures</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text>
          I spent 2 weeks in Magic Wood and Brione over August, did lots of scrambling and exploring, climbed a 7b (La Polka) and a 7b+ (Australian Open) and partially tore an ankle ligament on the penultimate day 🙏🔥<br />
          <strong>- Miranda</strong>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          My own climbing adventures were limited by a very busy summer, but a trip to the Dolomites saw President and Sister President on the Via Ferrata degli Alpini (photo below, #getthebadgein).
        </mj-text>
        <mj-image src="https://harryrich02.github.io/DUMC/img/harry-viaFerrata.jpg" width="400px" height="300px" alt="President and Sister President after Via Ferrata degli Alpini" />

        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold"
          >Preseason</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text>
          A great start to the season with nice and chill couple of sessions, having a bit of coaching towards the end. Thank to everyone that attended and a lesser thank you to those who told me to wear shorts on my first time outside (Leakey).</br>
          <strong>- Ethan</strong>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          The gang reconvened a week (or two for some) early for some preseason adventures. The week started with a bright and early 4pm start at Eden Rock for some training and mock trials. After a catch-up with the ever delightful Martha, a great session ensued culminating in a trip to the Swan on return to Durham. Day 2 saw a trip to Back Bowden, as featured in the wonderful <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dd7e01_IZl4/?stkn=MTdqdDQ0dmloMDFpZQ==" style="color: #7e317b; text-decoration: underline">edit</a> up on our Instagram. Trad and boulders were climbed, including President's second ever trad lead and first HVD.<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wednesday and Thursday consisted of Team Training at the DCC and a visit to Newcastle Climbing Centre for some lead. Of course, the most important event of the week was the bar-crawl on Thursday night. This led to a few hangovers the next day during exec training, with various cures attempted ranging from drowning their sorrows in milk to the more sensible hair of the dog method.<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A number of members competed at Eden Rock's Beast of Eden comp to great success. Very good performance from everyone attending the first competition of the year with lots of people coming in the top of the bunch! Finally to round out the week, a few brave souls travelled 2hrs down the country to find some dry rock, and were successful in their quest! Sport and a touch of shallow-water soloing completed a fantastic week!
        </mj-text>
        <mj-image src="https://harryrich02.github.io/DUMC/img/preseason-bowdenBouldering.jpg" width="225px" height="300px" alt="Preseason Bouldering at Back Bowden" />
        <mj-image src="https://harryrich02.github.io/DUMC/img/preseason-NCC.jpg" width="225px" height="300px" alt="Preseason Lead at NCC" />
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding-top="40px">
      <mj-column border="2px dashed #7E317B" border-radius="10px">
        <mj-text
          align="center"
          font-size="20px"
          font-weight="bold"
          color="#7E317B"
          >💪 WAD OF THE SUMMER</mj-text
        >
        <mj-text align="center" font-style="italic">
          Charlie for being struck by lightning?! (I wish I had more context)
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding-top="20px" padding-bottom="40px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text>
          <strong>Harry Richards</strong><br />
          DUMC President
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section background-color="#222222" padding="40px 20px">
      <mj-column vertical-align="middle">
        <mj-image
          width="120px"
          src="https://harryrich02.github.io/DUMC/img/dumcLogo.png"
          alt="DUMC Logo"
        />
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column vertical-align="middle">
        <mj-text
          color="#ffffff"
          font-size="14px"
          align="center"
          padding-bottom="10px"
        >
          <strong>Durham University Mountaineering Club</strong>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-social font-size="15px" icon-size="30px" mode="horizontal">
          <mj-social-element
            name="instagram"
            href="https://www.instagram.com/du.mountaineering"
            background-color="#7E317B"
          ></mj-social-element>
          <mj-social-element
            name="facebook"
            href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/DUMC.Forum"
            background-color="#7E317B"
          ></mj-social-element>
        </mj-social>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="13px" padding-top="15px">
          <a
            href="https://mountaineeringclub.webspace.durham.ac.uk/"
            style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: underline"
            >Visit our Website</a
          >
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
